diagrams2.key_results:
T1 census: one-loop 1PI graphs with P(eps,infty) edges. Count and FeynArts s; graph weight is 1/s, with s = |Aut| fixing the external legs.
- (A|_V,A|_V,A|_V), 11 graphs:
  - triangles with an A|_V, A|_{W^perp} or lambda loop, s=1 each;
  - two c-A^* loop triangles (opposite orientations), s=1;
  - bubbles g3[VVV]+g4[VVVV] and g3[VWW]+g4[VVWW], 3 channels each, s=2.
- (A|_V,A|_Wperp,A|_Wperp), 7 graphs:
  - triangles g3[VVV]g3[VWW]^2, g3[VWW]^3 and y[V]y[W]^2, s=1;
  - bubbles g3[VVV]+g4[VVWW] and g3[VWW]+g4[WWWW], s=2;
  - bubbles g3[VWW]+g4[VVWW] with a mixed A|_V/A|_{W^perp} loop, 2 channels, s=1.
- (lambda,lambda,A|_V): 4 triangles, s=1.
- (lambda,lambda,A|_Wperp): 4 triangles, s=1.
- (c,A|_V,A^*|_V): 2 triangles, g3[VVV]gh[V]^2 and gh[V]^3, s=1.
- (c,A|_Wperp,A^*|_Wperp): 1 triangle, g3[VWW]gh[V]gh[W].
- (c,lambda,lambda^*): 1 triangle, clamlams gh[V] y[V].
- (c,c,c^*): 1 triangle, cccs gh[V]^2.
- (A|_V)^4, 33 graphs:
  - 15 boxes (3 cyclic orders × loop of A|_V, A|_{W^perp}, lambda, and c-A^* in two orientations), s=1;
  - 12 triangles with one quartic vertex, s=1;
  - 6 bubbles, s=2.
- (A|_V)^2(A|_Wperp)^2, 25 graphs:
  - 9 boxes, 12 triangles;
  - 4 bubbles: two with s=2 (g4[VVVV]+g4[VVWW] and g4[VVWW]+g4[WWWW]) and two mixed-loop g4[VVWW]^2 with s=1.
- (A|_Wperp)^4, 27 graphs: 9 boxes, 12 triangles, 6 bubbles with s=2.
- omega: 1 for the (A|_V)^3 and A|_V(A|_Wperp)^2 sets, 0 for every other set.

T2 census, external (c, A|_V), omega=3:
- From (1/2)({I,I}_eps - {I,I}_0) there are five 1PI bubbles, s=1 each, each with one K_eps - K_0 edge and one P edge:
  - gh[V](c) + g3[VVV](A|_V): K-K0 A|_V->A^*|_V and P_AA(V);
  - gh[V](c) + gh[V](A|_V): K-K0 A|_V->A^*|_V and P_cA*;
  - gh[W](c) + g3[VWW](A|_V): K-K0 A|_W->A^*|_W and P_AA(W);
  - clamlams(c) + y[V](A|_V): K-K0 lambda->lambda^* and P_lamlam;
  - cccs(c) + gh[V](A|_V): K-K0 c->c^* and P_cA*.
- 4 tadpoles where K-K0 is the bridge, and 4 hbar Delta_eps I tadpoles with a K_eps self-loop. All 8 are zero, because the one-loop part is a g-invariant element of g.
- -Q I^CT[eps] enters as a single vertex with no edge.
- -{I,I^CT[eps]}_eps has no one-loop (c,A|_V) graph, since such a tree has at least 3 external legs.

Checks: the independent enumeration and the per-graph |Aut| agree with FeynArts for all 129 graphs. All 225 drawings match their FeynArts records.

Composites (25 groups, 179 panels):
- two-point A|_V (6); two-point A|_Wperp plus the A|_V–A|_Wperp graph (5); lambda and (c,A^*) (3);
- O1..O6 insertion graphs (6); L_eps boundary representatives (5): the A|_{W^perp} bubble pinned on either edge, and the O6 triangle pinned on each of its edges;
- one composite per cubic set (8);
- quartic boxes, triangles and bubbles for each of the three sets (9);
- T2 defect graphs (5) and their reducible tadpoles (8);
- route-(ii) K_eps graphs from round 1 (25: 21 loops and 4 counterterm trees).
- Each composites.json entry gives file, manuscript_path, title, and per panel: label, graph_id, rect [x,y,w,h] (fractions of the PNG, origin top-left, y downwards), and which drawing was used.

writer13.summary:
I wrote chapters 1-3 of the Step-1 manuscript using only the markup allowed by FORMAT.md. The preview wrapper compiles with xelatex in two passes into a 24-page PDF in manuscript/build. There are no errors, no undefined references and no missing glyphs; the widest leftover overfull box is 11pt.

Content comes from classical_spec.md and checks.json, superconformal/spec.md and verify.json, DEFINITIONS_v2 and the theory/notation audits in qa/, and every citation was checked against the primary-source texts. I followed DEFINITIONS_v2 items 1, 2, 5, 9, 10 and 11, and the replacements suggested in qa/audit_notation.md:
- no c_adj, u, B1-B7, N, tilde-P, r for the so(W_R^perp) element, I_3/I_4, slot brackets [A|_V], W_1 or S_free;
- the gauge algebra is g and the symmetry algebra is always written psl(4|4), with S^{(k)}_{psl(4|4)} abbreviated S^{(k)};
- supercharges always carry a subscript; generator types are named by index-free subspaces, and the [SW (8)] names appear only in one quotation column;
- Delta = 2E, with the conversion factor -2 to the Delta of [SW (3)];
- d_CE is the printed ESW formula times -1, with the reason given;
- both failing C07 axioms, (3) and (5), are stated with explicit components, plus the isotropy failure;
- the acyclicity theorem is followed by the remark on where the content of an operator lies;
- the random-draw verification is stated with explicit Schwartz-Zippel bounds, and uniqueness of S^(2) is listed as open.

Proofs give the explicit calculations: chirality via the Clifford relation; Q^2=0 and the adjointness of Q and Q^GF slot by slot; H checked component by component; the propagator components derived from L_t; QP=K_eps; the UV-boundary identity by induction on n; the homotopy identity with explicit heat-kernel bounds; the d_CE sign and the component equations through arity 3 with every shuffle sign; the brackets of the special conformal field, worked out in full; the tower ending at arity 2; and the one-loop formula for complex coefficients, proved by block reduction and a Zariski-density argument.

audits2.summary:
Adversarial notation and style audit of manuscript/ch01_classical.tex, ch02_superconformal.tex and ch03_uv_boundary.tex. The references were FORMAT.md, DEFINITIONS_v2 item 11, DESIGN rules 2 and 4, and ledger_SYNTHESIS.md. The audit found 76 findings (H 5, M 22, L 49). Each one has a file:line location and a compliant replacement, and all are written to qa/audit_notation2.json.

Citations that are not in the ledger were checked against the primary ESW PDF text and the C07 text: 13 were confirmed and 2 are not supported. The reader converter was dry-run in memory and no files were written. That run found three real rendering breakages:
- two labelled equations inside \item, which leaves unresolved references;
- 12 displays inside list items;
- double primes that get mangled in inline math.

The PDF build log was also checked for overfull boxes.
